Harm is stated plainly and kept behind closed doors: wounds, maimings, punishments, sacrifice, torture and atrocities are told at the level of fact ("one eye was lost", "a hand was cut off") or only implied ("the village was put to the sword", "what was done in that cellar was never spoken of"). Never describe them step by step: no anatomical or sadistic detail, nothing done to a body shown on the page, nothing gratuitous.
